                <pb facs="0723" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7670: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 12—8:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>573. From Admiral McCully [,Sevastopol?]:</p>
                <p>“90. November 11, 10 p.m. Evacuation of Crimea inevitable and Sevastopol may hold
                    out another week but hardly longer. I propose <pb facs="0724" n="624"
                        xml:id="pg624"/> to evacuate all Americans, American citizens, and proceed
                    to Constantinople unless otherwise instructed. McCully.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
